    "title": "Illinois coach Brad Underwood shrugs off Houston's Sweet 16 advantage",
    "text": "Head coach Brad Underwood of the Illinois Fighting Illini cheers on his players in the second half during a college basketball game against the Penn State Nittany Lions at the Palestra on Jan. 3, 2026, in Philadelphia, Pennsylvania.Mitchell Layton/Getty ImagesIllinois coach Brad Underwood has no issues playing against the Houston Cougars in their backyard.He’s had to drive much farther.Article continues below this adGet Digital Access and Stay Informed With Trusted Local News.Get Digital Access and Stay Informed With Trusted Local News.ONLY 25¢“I’ll be honest, I (couldn’t) care less,” Underwood said Wednesday. “I’m going to sound really selfish here. I’m an old JUCO ball coach. I drove 16-passenger vans. I drove from Dodge City, Kansas, to Mesa, Arizona, for a basketball tournament in a bus. If you would have told me back then that I’m getting to coach basketball in the Sweet 16 and play Houston, I would sign up for it. I would crawl to get there.”As the No. 2 seed, Houston was placed in the South Region, which will host the Sweet 16 and Elite Eight at Toyota Center. The drive is a little more than two miles from the UH campus.Zvonimir Ivisic #44 of the Illinois Fighting Illini speaks with the media during the Sweet Sixteen Practice Day at Toyota Center on March 25, 2026, in Houston, Texas. Kenneth Richmond/Getty ImagesThat has sparked discussion about whether the Houston Cougars' placement in the hometown regional is fair and whether it gives the Cougars a home-court advantage.Article continues below this ad“We’re not worried about the crowd,” Illini center Zvonimir Ivisic said. “We expected it was going to be a good crowd here. We play Houston. We don’t play the fans.”UH positioned itself to play close to home by relinquishing its host-school duties to Rice last summer. From there, the Cougars finished second in the Big 12 and were considered for the last No. 1 seed. Florida was the South’s top seed until an upset loss to Iowa in the second round.Article continues below this adDon't miss news and stories you need to read.",
